{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3224","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3224","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3224\",\"parent_revision\":\"9e07e5010e4b533d75cb73aca552d0b6b54e7cd04ccec4590d5779d4eb39cfe1\",\"root_revision\":\"9e07e5010e4b533d75cb73aca552d0b6b54e7cd04ccec4590d5779d4eb39cfe1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-24\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe repo's primary checkout filesystem was measured at 100% full (`df -h .` showed 73MB available on a 234G volume) mid-session, which caused a `git worktree add` invocation for a new agent worktree to fail with \\\"No space left on device\\\". `git worktree list` showed 134 worktrees; `du -sh .claude/worktrees` measured 56GB in that directory alone.\\n\\nCross-referencing each worktree's checked-out branch against `git ls-remote --heads origin` found 105 worktrees whose branch no longer exists on the remote (their PR was merged or closed and the branch deleted). Of those, only 11 were both clean (`git status --porcelain` empty) and had zero commits absent from `origin/main` (`git rev-list --count <branch> ^origin/main`) \u2014 those 11 were removed in-session via `git worktree remove --force` to unblock the immediate task, freeing the volume from 73MB to 2.4GB available.\\n\\nThe remaining ~94 worktrees are NOT confirmed safe to remove: each either has uncommitted changes, or has commits `git rev-list` does not find as ancestors of `origin/main` \u2014 but that ancestor check produces false negatives for squash-merged PRs (content already landed on `main` via a squash commit, so the branch's original commits are legitimately absent from `main`'s history even though nothing is lost). A trustworthy safe-to-remove determination for those 94 requires per-worktree diff-level comparison against `main` (e.g. whether `git diff main...<branch>` is empty, or whether the corresponding PR/issue shows a merged state via `gh pr list --state merged`), not a simple ancestor check.\\n\\nAdditionally, 15 worktrees repo-wide were found to have uncommitted changes (`git status --porcelain` non-empty) via a separate sweep \u2014 those must not be touched by any cleanup pass without first confirming with whoever owns that work.\\n\\nUser-provided context: user chose to remove only the 11 trivially-safe worktrees immediately and file this item for the rest, rather than pause active PR-rebase work for a full audit or run the full audit inline.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session discovering /Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills disk at 100% (73MB free) while dispatching PR-rebase subagents on 2026-08-24\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f65f78a42296c469f3f4ca281ac96e75c555765d4b771f34320b738530ba3c76\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQg4UDw\"}"}